WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:11.240
A 2018 Pew poll reports that a majority
of Americans on both the right and the left

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:15.960
say that higher education is headed
in the wrong direction – and they're spot on.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.160
On the left, respondents say tuition
costs are too high.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:23.040
While college presidents have made
excuses and pointed fingers,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.240
after-inflation costs have more than doubled
over the past 30 years, as colleges

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.800
cheerfully spent heavily on amenities,
athletics, and bureaucracy.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:37.080
On the right, those who see things going south
point to politicized classrooms and

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:42.100
restrictions on campus speech. Behind the
many instances where Republican

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.960
sentiment has been treated as a thought
crime on campus is the inconvenient

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:49.840
reality that liberal faculty outnumber
conservatives five to one,

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:55.140
and that one in three sociologists admit 
they'd be less likely to hire a new professor

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.619
if he or she was a Republican.
While there's little evidence that

00:00:58.619 --> 00:01:03.059
public censure will prompt needed change
on campus, it's reassuring to know that

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.660
Americans on both sides of the aisle are
seeing things clearly.

00:01:08.620 --> 00:01:13.900
Do you think America's colleges are headed in the
wrong direction? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.330
Also let us know what other
topics you'd like our scholars to cover

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:26.540
in 60 seconds and be sure to LIKE and
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

